WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.183
- Hi, my name is Matthias Schweighöfer,

00:00:02.183 --> 00:00:06.007
and I'm the lead actor of this film,

00:00:06.007 --> 00:00:06.840
"Army of Thieves,"

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.430
and the director of this film.

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:10.300
- I'm Zack Snyder.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.787
I am the producer and
I wrote the story for

00:00:13.787 --> 00:00:15.189
"Army of Thieves."

00:00:15.189 --> 00:00:17.664
(suspenseful music)

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.010
If you are watching "Army of the Dead,"

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.730
you'll notice that in the timeline

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:32.623
we're probably right alongside
of "Army of Thieves."

00:00:32.623 --> 00:00:34.214
(intense music)

00:00:34.214 --> 00:00:35.650
(rewind)

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:38.500
Because what happens within
the body of the film,

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.521
we see the fall of Vegas,

00:00:40.521 --> 00:00:44.140
which, as you know, we
see in the title sequence

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.060
of "Army of the Dead."

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.490
Just as Vegas is falling,

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:51.530
our team in Germany are
cracking these safes.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.530
- [Korina] We've assembled
from various sources

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:56.000
the locations of the three safes.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.080
- So there's this legendary
Ring Cycle, you know,

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.610
and it's four safes made by Hans Wagner.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:07.130
You know what this is
like a family of safes

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.860
guiding us to, you know,

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.940
the lost dear friend,

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.670
somewhere in America.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:17.240
- All the safes are owned by Bly Tanaka,

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.983
who is the guy who owns the Bly Casino

00:01:20.983 --> 00:01:23.370
that they end up going to in Las Vegas.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:26.570
- [Scott] How would you
like to make 250-grand,

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:27.960
for one day's work?

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:28.860
- Oh, my god.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.610
- We had written this whole concept for

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.950
Dieter to explain the Ring Cycle safes

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.630
in "Army of the Dead."

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:40.480
The scene as written is
probably another, like,

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.390
three or four minutes longer--

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:43.760
just the speech.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.234
- He named it the Götterdämmerung

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:48.516
for the final chapter in his namesake

00:01:48.516 --> 00:01:50.600
Richard Wagner's epic opera.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.969
- It was Matthias doing the scene

00:01:52.969 --> 00:01:54.957
that made me go, like, "Oh, yeah."

00:01:54.957 --> 00:01:56.870
Finding out why that character is

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:58.985
so obsessed with safes is a thing,

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.450
I think, that's fun.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.090
And that's really how it started.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:05.160
- He was talking about the
potential idea of a spinoff

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.620
and about Dieter

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.210
and I was like,

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:09.750
"What? What did you just say?"

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:13.068
Then he offered me the
film to be the director,

00:02:13.068 --> 00:02:14.860
and I was like, (kissing)

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:15.900
"Thank you. I will do this.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:16.733
Is that true?"

00:02:16.733 --> 00:02:17.566
And he said,

00:02:18.566 --> 00:02:19.399
- [Both] "Yes."

00:02:19.399 --> 00:02:20.640
- "It's very true."

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.990
- You're in?

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.232
- We'll go through it together.

00:02:23.232 --> 00:02:24.723
(upbeat music)

00:02:24.723 --> 00:02:26.289
- Is it like in a movie film,

00:02:26.289 --> 00:02:28.310
where each one of us has
a different skill set,

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:29.885
and it's only working together

00:02:29.885 --> 00:02:33.110
that we can pull off that
which needs the pulling off?

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:35.240
- We do sort of investigate the tropes

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.032
and kind of play with the ideas

00:02:37.032 --> 00:02:38.630
of, like, a heist film.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:41.982
There's nothing tropier
than the joining of the team

00:02:41.982 --> 00:02:43.870
and a creation of the team.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:46.590
And sort of the description
of the skill sets

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:47.930
of the team members.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:51.436
That's, like, one of the main linchpins of

00:02:51.436 --> 00:02:53.220
making a heist film.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.053
That was fun,

00:02:54.053 --> 00:02:55.730
and then throwing Dieter,

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.370
this innocent Dieter,

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:59.692
into the mix with these kind of, like,

00:02:59.692 --> 00:03:02.520
badass thieves was really--

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:03.982
that was really fun to talk about.

00:03:03.982 --> 00:03:05.095
- Wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wait!

00:03:05.095 --> 00:03:05.928
Wa, wa wait.

00:03:05.928 --> 00:03:06.977
(squeals)

00:03:06.977 --> 00:03:09.050
- To create a character (chuckles)

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:12.130
that has to be protected by a whole team,

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:14.265
and everyone in the team knows,

00:03:14.265 --> 00:03:16.850
you know, "I don't know how
the fuck we can do this."

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:19.084
To have a foundation for
a character like this,

00:03:19.084 --> 00:03:21.530
protect him because we need him.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:22.363
- Behind me.

00:03:23.873 --> 00:03:25.703
- Hold this please.

00:03:25.703 --> 00:03:26.536
(punch thudding)

00:03:26.536 --> 00:03:28.090
- It's a dream coming
true for a character.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:28.923
Boom.

00:03:28.923 --> 00:03:31.100
- It's not a zombie movie, per se.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.630
I mean, you might get a taste but,

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:34.463
you know.

00:03:34.463 --> 00:03:35.590
- If you never heard about,

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.009
you know, like, "Army of Thieves"

00:03:37.009 --> 00:03:38.600
or "Army of the Dead,"

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:40.170
you can be happy just, you know,

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.947
there is a prequel and a sequel

00:03:41.947 --> 00:03:44.530
if you explore these films totally new.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.270
- Unfortunately, you're
just gonna have to endure

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:48.835
these incredible actors,

00:03:48.835 --> 00:03:52.068
cracking safes and fighting
their way through Europe

00:03:52.068 --> 00:03:53.850
on this amazing adventure.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:54.810
- My god,

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:55.643
there's a prequel.

00:03:55.643 --> 00:03:58.530
Or, there is a sequel to the prequel,

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.110
and there will be more?

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:01.548
I'm going crazy!

00:04:01.548 --> 00:04:02.456
- So...

00:04:02.456 --> 00:04:03.497
Sorry about that.

